        "quiz_type": "single_choice",
        "question_type": "single_choice",
        "question_title": "Using Heron's formula, find the area of a triangle whose side lengths are \\(13\\text{ cm}\\), \\(14\\text{ cm}\\), and \\(15\\text{ cm}\\).",
        "question_instruction": "Choose one correct option.",
        "explanation": "The semiperimeter is \\(s=\\frac{13+14+15}{2}=21\\text{ cm}\\). Hence, \\(S=\\sqrt{s(s-13)(s-14)(s-15)}=\\sqrt{21\\cdot8\\cdot7\\cdot6}=84\\text{ cm}^2\\).",
        "question_audio": null,
        "time_limit_seconds": 30,
        "points": 10,
        "sort_order": 127,
        "question_data": {
